[8] Date: 2023-01-09 | Status: todo | Section: description | Editor: SUPPLIER
BEFORE: {"description":"Fill your evening with romance on a walking tour of Vilnius and hear stories of love through the ages. Start near the Cathedral of Vilnius in one of the largest surviving medieval old towns in Northern Europe.\n\nHear spicy, sensual, strange and sometimes tragic love stories with connections to the city's buildings, streets and parks. Delve deeper than the famous story of the Grand Duke of Lithuania, Žygimantas Augustas and his wife Barbara Radziwiłł and discover some lesser-known tales.\n\nStroll through the Old Town learning who broke the heart of Tsarina’s lover, and in what weird way the future French ambassador expressed his love. Find out what charming spell a Venetian tavern singer used to seduce famous Lithuanian noblemen. Stroll by moonlight to bring these touching stories to life and perhaps renew or inspire new love sensations of your own."}
AFTER: {"description":"Discover the city on a private tour made just for you. An exclusive tour for all the romantics of the world! Take a romantic walking tour for couples around Vilnius. Discover the love stories hidden in the city’s charming streets, parks, and buildings. Together with the professional local guide, you will visit the most romantic places in the city. You will feel spellbound in a vibrant atmosphere. What is considered as one of the best places to have a date in the city? Where can you take lovely photos? Where can you enjoy a few romantic moments with your partner? Along the way, you will have the chance to stop and admire breathtaking sights of the city. This is a perfect way to spend a romantic day in Vilnius."}

