BEFORE: {"description":"Have an experienced guide help you to explore the city of Kaunas. Kaunas Old Town is located in the intersection of the two largest rivers of Lithuania. The medieval defender of Lithuania – Kaunas Castle now remains the heart of the city. The city was created near it.\n\nThe Franciscan brothers, Bernardines and Jesuits have all worked there and have left the most beautiful religious buildings in the city (St. George, Vytautas and the Jesuit Church).\n\nFrom here, the only city in Lithuania, the Hanseatic merchants built trading routes. Footprints of Jewish culture left in the city as well as other famous people who lived in Kaunas will also be mentioned. "}
