BEFORE: {"description":"Discover all you can about Vilnius, when was it born, who created it and so much more. The professional guide will tell You the facts You need to know about the capital of Lithuania. You will hear an interesting and mysterious legend about Vilnius. What an unusual dream had Great Duke Gediminas? How is this related to the birth of the capital? \n\n\nHear about the life of Vilnius citizens in the old times. Which buildings still remain, why the windows were not built on the main street side.\n\nDuring this tour, you will learn how the Great Duke was taking care of the capital. Find out what innovations queen Bona brought to Lithuania and the biggest spring festival in Vilnius. Why does it rock the city each year?"}
AFTER: {"description":"Step into the majestic heart of Vilnius, where centuries of royal influence and cultural heritage have shaped one of Europe’s most elegant Old Towns. This private walking tour invites you to discover a city whose history stretches far beyond that of the United States, reflected in its classical architecture, grand squares, and historic landmarks.\n\nWith a professional local guide, explore the most significant sites that define Vilnius as a former center of power, religion, and artistic expression. Walk through Cathedral Square, where the foundations of Lithuanian identity were established, and continue along historic streets lined with baroque and neoclassical buildings that reveal the city’s royal past.\n\nAs the journey unfolds, you will uncover stories of rulers, cultural transformation, and architectural achievements that shaped the city across generations. Each stop offers a deeper understanding of Vilnius as a living reflection of European civilization.\n\nThis refined and immersive experience is designed for travelers who value history, culture, and architectural beauty, offering an elegant way to explore Vilnius through its majestic and royal legacy.\n\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

