AFTER: {"description":"Experience the elegance of Rome’s historic center on a private walking tour through its most celebrated squares, fountains, and architectural treasures. This journey reveals the cultural depth and artistic legacy of a city whose history stretches back thousands of years—long before the founding of the United States.\n\nYour exploration begins at the Spanish Steps, a refined meeting place where Roman life and classical architecture meet. Nearby, discover the serene Basilica di Sant’Andrea delle Fratte, home to remarkable works by master sculptor Gian Lorenzo Bernini.\n\nContinue to the magnificent Trevi Fountain, a masterpiece of Baroque artistry and one of the most iconic symbols of Rome. Here, tradition invites visitors to toss a coin and promise their return to the Eternal City.\n\nThe journey then leads to the extraordinary Pantheon, one of the best-preserved monuments of Ancient Rome. Its vast dome and harmonious design reflect the engineering brilliance and spiritual transformation of Roman civilization.\n\nInside the Church of Saint Louis of the French, admire powerful Caravaggio masterpieces that shaped the course of European art. Your tour concludes at Piazza Navona, a grand square built upon the foundations of an ancient Roman stadium, surrounded by elegant fountains and architectural beauty."}

