BEFORE: {"description":"Admire all the wonders Managua has to offer on this 4-hour guided city highlights tour. From the lively city center to the breathtaking views from the Tiscapa Lagoon, discover the history behind every turn with your local guide.\n\nStart your walking adventure at the Ruben Dario Monument, make a turn and see the Ruben Dario National Theatre. Learn about the powerful cultural and literary influence of Ruben Dario from your guide as you stroll.\n\nContinue to Plaza la Fe and see the statue of Simon Bolivar, a figure of independence and revolution throughout South America. Enter the bustling city center and explore Parque Central and the historical Plaza de la Revolución.\n\nFrom here, make your way to the Casa Presidential and see the main office of the president. Arrive at the Old Cathedral and marvel at the neoclassical architecture.\n\nVisit the National Palace of Culture, formally a royal residence, and see the Roosevelt Monument. Then, arrive at the Tiscapa Lagoon for stunning views of Managua before finishing your tour at the Metropolitan Cathedral of the Immaculate Conception."}
AFTER: {"description":"Managua is the capital of Nicaragua and is home to a rich and diverse history. A historical walking tour of Managua is the perfect way to explore the city and its many attractions. Visit some of Managua’s most iconic landmarks, such as the Palacio Nacional and the National Cathedral. Scroll through some of the city’s best outdoor markets and other historic sites. Along the way, your guide will provide interesting anecdotes and stories about Managua’s past, giving you a deeper understanding of the city’s rich culture and history. Tourists should visit Managua to experience the unique fusion of pre–Columbian, colonial, and modern culture, as well as the vibrant energy of this bustling Central American city. Be part of this tour and create memories that will last a lifetime!"}

