BEFORE: {"description":"Get ready to experience Panama’s capital from a different perspective on this private guided walking tour. Follow a local as they show you the best of Panama City while revealing interesting facts. Visit Palacio de las Garzas (Herons' Palace), Bolivar Park, and more.\n\nExplore Panama City like a local as you visit Iglesia de San Francisco de Asis (church), Teatro Nacional (National Theater), and many other top sights.\n\nStart by meeting in Casco Antiguo, Panama’s historic district. Later, continue the tour to the must-see Plaza de Francia (French Plaza) with its statues and large stone tablets.\n\nGaze at the Catedral Metropolitana (Metropolitan Cathedral), which is one of the largest in Central America. The cathedral was designed by military engineers and completed in 1796.\n\nBefore the end of the tour, you’ll get to discover Casco Viejo, an area that features a unique mix of architectural styles, each revealing a certain part of the country’s eventful history."}
AFTER: {"description":"This private cultural walking tour reveals the rich heritage and architectural splendor of Casco Antiguo, the historic heart of Panama City and a UNESCO Heritage treasure. Explore the beautifully preserved Old Town, where centuries of history, cultural exchange, and architectural excellence have created one of Latin America’s most captivating historic districts. Wander through charming plazas and historic streets that reflect the city’s remarkable transformation over time.\n\nWhat stories of explorers, merchants, and civilizations shaped this strategic crossroads of the Americas? Your experienced guide will share fascinating insights into Casco Antiguo’s cultural legacy, historical significance, and architectural heritage. Admire elegant colonial buildings, historic churches, and landmark sites that showcase the enduring influence of Spanish and regional traditions.\n\nWith roots extending centuries before the foundations of the United States, Casco Antiguo offers an inspiring journey through the rise of trade, cultural exchange, and urban development in the Americas. This premium experience combines UNESCO-recognized heritage, architectural beauty, and historical discovery, providing a deeper appreciation of one of Panama’s most distinguished cultural destinations.\n\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

