BEFORE: {"description":"Embark on a historic walk into the top sights that Old San Juan has to offer. Experience San Juan from a local's perspective as your guide walks you through the most notable landmarks. Marvel at the colorful Spanish colonial architecture dating back to the 16th and 17th centuries. See beautiful historical buildings such as the Cathedral of San Juan Bautista, one of the oldest buildings in San Juan.\n\nVisit the 16th century El Morro and La Fortaleza fortresses that are rising above the ocean, and then stroll along the Paseo de la Princesa, taking in the stunning views of the bay. Learn about the importance of Christopher Columbus for Puerto Rico, find out what was San Juan's original name, and hear about the Spanish-American post-war history. Then together with your local guide find out what’s inside San Juan’s San Felipe del Morro citadel."}
AFTER: {"description":"Enjoy a private, exclusive tour with your own local guide as you explore the historic charm of Old San Juan. Walk through colorful streets filled with colonial architecture, vibrant plazas, and centuries-old landmarks that reflect Puerto Rico’s rich cultural heritage. Discover the stories behind iconic sites like El Morro, La Fortaleza, and the scenic Paseo de la Princesa while learning how history shaped the island. Hear about Christopher Columbus and the transformation of San Juan over time, including events that defined its identity. Stroll along cobblestone paths where past and present blend seamlessly, offering a unique perspective on this historic city. Your knowledgeable guide will share engaging insights, making every stop meaningful and memorable. This immersive experience is perfect for travelers seeking culture, history, and authentic local stories in a relaxed, private setting."}

