BEFORE: {"description":"Bulgaria’s capital Sofia has many stories to tell, which are fascinating even for those without much of a passion for history. The city itself is also beautiful to look at, and throughout this tour you will enjoy the fanciest street in the city, Vitosha Boulevard.\n\nThere you can shop in the posh boutiques and fashion houses before enjoying lunch at a folklore-themed restaurant. Alternatively, you can head up to one of the many rooftop bars for a drink. If you are a lover of Neoclassical architecture, The Ivan Vazov National Theatre is another fantastic part of Bulgarian culture.\n\nSophia is also home to one of the oldest parks in Europe, which you will be free to take a scenic wonder through during this experience. Other sites you will be free to encounter on this tour include Borisova Gradina, the Serdica Amphitheatre, and the Central Mineral Baths, all of which will be accompanied by secret stories of this beautiful city."}
AFTER: {"description":"Sofia‘s gardens offer visitors a unique and private opportunity to escape the hustle and bustle of the city and explore the natural beauty of the city. With its lush green lawns and picturesque pathways, it‘s the perfect place to take a leisurely stroll, enjoy a picnic, or simply relax and take in the scenery. The gardens are home to a variety of native trees, plants, and flowers, and you can spot some rare species and vibrant colors throughout the gardens. The gardens also feature a variety of sculptures, monuments, and fountains, making it a truly enchanting place to explore. No trip to Sofia is complete without a visit to the gardens. Tourists will be able to enjoy a peaceful and serene atmosphere, observe the local wildlife, and take in the history and culture of the city. Whether it‘s a day out with the family or a romantic evening stroll, Sofia‘s gardens are sure to provide a memorable experience for all. This garden tour of Sofia is sure to be etched in your memories forever!"}

