BEFORE: {"description":"Bratislava is Slovakia's capital, and is situated just 60 kilometers from the Austrian capital of Vienna near the Danube River. The city has changed its name five times, and throughout this tour you will discover many places of interest such as Town Hall, the Primatial Palace, Martin’s Cathedral, Bratislava Castle, and St. Michael’s Gate.\n\nNo tour to Bratislava is complete without tasting the city's food and drinks. Bratislava has a big variety of places where you can enjoy potatoes, dumplings, thick sauces, and cheeses. You'll have the opportunity to sample a plum brandy called Slivovica, as your experienced guide takes you around the best places to try Slovak cuisine.\n\nYou will get to meet craft producers and beer makers, and will not only taste unique dishes like Kofola, Treska v majonéze, Kapustnica, Bryndzové halusky, but will also hear stories about how these dishes became so popular. Towards the end of your tour you can also try the popular Slovakian blackcurrant wine and honey wine."}
AFTER: {"description":"his private walking tour reveals the cultural richness and historic character of Bratislava, a city shaped by centuries of European civilization, royal influence, and architectural achievement. Explore the charming Old Town, where medieval streets, elegant squares, and historic landmarks tell the story of a destination that stood at the crossroads of cultures and empires. Discover how Bratislava evolved through centuries of political and cultural transformation while preserving its unique identity.\n\nAdmire heritage landmarks and architectural masterpieces that reflect Bratislava’s important role in Central European history. With roots extending deep into Europe’s past, long before the foundations of the United States, Bratislava offers an inspiring journey through centuries of culture, tradition, and transformation. This premium experience combines cultural discovery, historical storytelling, and architectural beauty in one of Europe’s most captivating historic capitals.\n\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience.\nYou will also get to experience the following attractions:\n- Michael's Gate\n- Bratislava Old Town Hall\n- St. Martin's Cathedral\n- Bratislava Castle"}

