BEFORE: {"description":"Discover the beautiful city of Geneva during a fascinating walking tour with a charismatic local guide. Not only the cradle of watchmaking and home to the greatest Swiss chocolate makers, but Geneva also promises you an original and enriching experience. Meet your guide in downtown Geneva and set off together on your guided tour. As you stroll through the historic streets, admire the medieval look and marvelous architecture, which mixes both French and German influences. \n\nSee the headquarters for notable international organizations including the WTO and the United Nations. Also, discover the headquarters of the World Intellectual Property Organisation, Telecommunication Organization, and UNHCR, and the Red Cross Institution. Finally, pay a visit to the magnificent Ariana Museum for the opportunity to marvel at the incredible glass and ceramic collections."}
AFTER: {"description":"This private walking tour reveals Geneva’s historic heritage shaped long before the United States. Step into an ancient city where medieval streets reflect centuries of European civilization and cultural transformation. What stories emerge from Geneva’s architectural and cultural legacy?\n\nExplore a museum that preserves artistic and historical heritage across generations. Admire a grand cathedral built above archaeological remains that reveal ancient foundations. Walk through a historic park where a monumental wall reflects religious transformation and intellectual influence. Discover refined architecture that represents Geneva’s cultural evolution through time.\n\nThe journey concludes in a space where historic industry meets modern cultural expression. Each step connects you to heritage, architecture, and the legacy of civilization shaped over centuries.\n\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

