BEFORE: {"description":"When Christmas time knocks on the doors, the always-fascinating Copenhagen turns into a box full of surprises. Colorful streets, intriguing stories, vibrant holiday atmosphere, local delicacies, a plethora of monuments, and unique heritage are only some reasons why Copenhagen is definitely a place to visit and experience during the Christmas period. Through a 2-hour walking tour, explore and discover Copenhagen's charming Christmas spirits as you witness some of the most inspiring areas in the city. Explore local traditions and customs at the fascinating Tivoli Gardens, enjoy scenes at the iconic Hajbro Plads Square, experience the authentic atmosphere at Stork Fountain, and discover local traditions at Nytorv Square."}
AFTER: {"description":"Step into Copenhagen’s festive charm on this private walking tour. You stroll past the glittering lights of Tivoli Gardens, feeling crisp winter air on your cheeks. The scent of pine and mulled spices drifts from nearby stalls as your guide shares stories of Danish Christmas traditions. At Hajbro Plads Square, the Christmas Market invites you to wander among wooden stalls adorned with garlands and twinkling lights. The Stork Fountain sparkles in the frosty light while locals chat and laughter echoes across the square. At Nytorv Square, the ice rink glimmers as skaters twirl beneath glowing lanterns. You sip warm gløgg and take in the magical atmosphere, the city alive with festive energy.\n\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

