BEFORE: {"description":"Get an insider’s view of Callanish on the Isle of Lewis on a 2-hour group walking tour of the Calanais Standing Stones and the village.\n\nMeet your local guide directly at the Calanais Standing Stones and dive straight into the historical importance of this extraordinary cross-shaped setting of stones erected 5,000 years ago.\n\nLearn about the mysterious long-standing stones from your expert guide, hearing stories and legends of its inception. Many believe it was most likely an astronomical observatory and a place of ritual activity for over 2,000 years, but its true beginnings are still unknown.\n\nContinue your journey with a visit to the nearby village of Callanish, a typical and charming Outer Hebrides township."}
AFTER: {"description":"This private walking tour explores Callanish Stone Circles, a prehistoric heritage site shaped by ancient civilization and archaeological legacy. You step into the Hebridean landscape where historic Old Town meets mystical Neolithic monuments. What stories do these standing stones hold across thousands of years?\n\nYou walk among the Callanish Standing Stones, where architectural alignment and classical celestial design reflect early human understanding of time and space. At Callanish II and III, smaller stone circles reveal cultural heritage and ritual significance linked to ancient civilization. The open landscape enhances the sense of cultural depth and transformation shaped by prehistoric communities.\n\nEach stop brings you closer to Scotland’s ancient legacy, where stone monuments preserve stories of civilization and ritual life. Please note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

