BEFORE: {"description":"An exclusive tour for all the romantics of the world! Together with the professional local guide, you will visit the most romantic places in the city. If you pass away in Amsterdam but don’t have any family, friends or acquaintances, then a poet will write a poem and recite it on your funeral. You will feel spellbound in a charming atmosphere. What is considered as one of the best places to have a date in the city? Where can you make lovely photos? You will be surprised how many historical love stories are hidden in the streets, buildings, parks of the city. From heartbreaking and tragic, to the hilarious or spicy ones. The Red-Light District is well known for its red lights, however, there are also blue lights. When the lights are blue you know that there is a transgender woman in the room. What’s worth knowing about the love story of Henry and Katherine Hudsons? This tour is especially recommended in the Saint Valentine period!"}
AFTER: {"description":"Enjoy a private walking tour through Amsterdam’s historic Old Town. Discover a cultural landscape shaped by centuries of European civilization. Oude Kerk reveals medieval origins and ancient architectural heritage. Centraal Station presents a grand example of classical design and urban transformation. Dam Square reflects political history and cultural evolution.\nThe Royal Palace showcases baroque architecture and royal legacy. Westerkerk stands as a symbol of religious and architectural heritage. Walk near the Anne Frank House and reflect on powerful moments of history. The Tulip Museum highlights botanical traditions within Dutch cultural identity. The port reveals Amsterdam’s role in global trade and civilization growth.\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience.."}

