BEFORE: {"description":"Enjoy a private, exclusive tour with your own local guide. Discover the city of Venice and admire its iconic landmarks on a guided walking tour. See famous places like St. Mark’s Basilica, the Doge's Palace, the Bridge of Sighs, and the Rialto Bridge.\n\nStart your walking tour at the stunning St. Mark’s Basilica, a masterpiece of Byzantine architecture, and learn about its rich history and the relics it houses. Next, see the Doge’s Palace, a symbol of Venice’s power and splendor throughout the ages.\n\nWalk across the iconic Bridge of Sighs, connecting the palace with the new prisons, and then head to the bustling Rialto Bridge, the oldest of the bridges spanning the Grand Canal.\n\nVisit the Basilica dei Santi Giovanni e Paolo, one of the city’s largest churches, famed for its impressive Gothic structure. Admire the Equestrian statue of Bartolomeo Colleoni, a tribute to one of Venice’s great military leaders.\n\nConclude your tour at St. Mark's Square, absorbing the festive atmosphere and the architectural beauty that surrounds you."}
AFTER: {"description":"This private walking tour invites you to discover the historic heart of Venice through its most celebrated architectural landmarks. Begin in St Mark’s Square where medieval power and maritime civilization shaped a legacy older than the United States. Enter St Mark’s Basilica and admire luminous mosaics that reflect Byzantine artistry and sacred tradition. Continue to the Doge’s Palace where governance and diplomacy defined a republic that influenced Europe. Cross the Bridge of Sighs and reflect on stories of justice and transformation. Conclude at the Rialto Bridge where classical engineering still connects daily Venetian life. Your licensed guide ensures cultural depth and seamless navigation throughout.\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

