AFTER: {"description":"This private romantic walking tour explores Santo Domingo Old Town, a UNESCO Heritage site where history older than the United States unfolds through colonial streets. You walk through an ancient cultural landscape shaped by civilization and transformation, where architectural and classical influences define every corner. Zona Colonial reveals layers of archaeological and medieval heritage, reflecting the city’s deep cultural legacy. What stories of love and devotion were born within these historic walls?\n\nYou move through Columbus Park, surrounded by classical architecture and vibrant cultural life, while your guide shares inspiring narratives of romance and historical connection. At Fortaleza Ozama, one of the oldest European-built fortresses in the Americas, you experience the strength of early civilization and its enduring legacy. Each stop reflects architectural heritage and the evolution of Santo Domingo as a historic cultural center.\n\nPlease note: The program and attractions may vary based on booking date/time and crowd conditions, ensuring each visit is a unique experience."}

