BEFORE: {"description":"Let's make the best tour ever in Split! The first attraction in Split is Diocletian Palace and peristyle. Just after resting in a coffee shop, we reach the symbol of Split town St.Duje Cathedral with a bell tower 57m high built in the 13th century. If you want a unique view of the entire city and the central Dalmatian islands, you should climb to the top. The cathedral is in front of the Peristyle square. Peristyle Square, through the narrowest street, takes you to Jupiter’s temple. Leave Diocletian Palace through Bronze Gate and Finish your tour in Riva- the Split waterfront- iconic place and a favorite meeting point for locals.!"}
AFTER: {"description":"The Fascinating Heritage of Split is a 2-hour program led by a local guide who is enthusiastic about the hometown. You will explore and discover some of the most exciting aspects and corners of Split. Why is there a black Sphynx? What was Diocletian's favorite hobby? What does the inside of the Palace hide? Why did the Romans build the secret tunnel to the center of the city? You will be charmed by the antique atmosphere of old Split. We'll walk down antique historical streets and suddenly find ourselves stepping back into ancient Roman times. Then we witness gems and heritage of Venetian history before we step foot into the modern area of the charming Split. The mix of rushing times comes together with interesting legends and stories delivered by the local guide."}

