[5] Date: 2022-12-01 | Status: todo | Section: description | Editor: SUPPLIER
BEFORE: {"description":"Taking a walking tour in Belém will open up new horizons. The architecture and the history of this district are pretty inspiring, and you will discover it all in detail throughout this experience.\n\nBelem is a district of Lisbon located not far from the main city center sights., and whilst there your local charismatic guide will reveal interesting facts about Portuguese history. Whist visiting Belém's monuments, you will get to learn everything about Portuguese history including how it once was a world power. You'll also learn why Belém is one of the most important areas of Lisbon, and why it was important for the famous explorers Christopher Columbus, Vasco da Gama, and Pedro Álvares Cabral.\n\nLater, discover why Mosteiro dos Jerónimos has been proclaimed as World Heritage by UNESCO, before becoming familiar with the Santa Maria de Belém. At the conclusion of your scenic and educational experience, you'll result at the Overseas Oeiras Garden."}
AFTER: {"description":"Embark on a captivating two-hour walking tour of Lisbon’s charming Belem district, where history and architectural wonders await. Begin by exploring the Garden of Afonso de Albuquerque, a tranquil oasis perfect for a leisurely stroll. Then, marvel at the grandeur of Palácio Nacional de Belém, the official residence of the Portuguese President, with its impressive architecture and regal presence. Next, immerse yourself in the beauty of the Tropical Botanical Garden, a paradise of exotic plants and vibrant flora. Then pass by the Hieronymites Monastery, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its stunning Manueline architecture and historical significance. Admire the Monument Gago Coutinho e Sacadura Cabral, a tribute to the brave aviators who made history with their transatlantic flight. Witness the iconic Belem Tower, a symbol of Lisbon’s maritime past, and pass by the Belem Lighthouse, a maritime landmark that has guided ships along the coast for years."}

